s to be outside of time and space  the Titan transformation appears to take  place instantly within the physical  world as of chapter 120 it appears that  Zeke is the only one who can command  Amir as a result of his royal blood even  though the power of the founding Titan  currently resides with him Eren he  cannot command Amir because he doesn't  have royal blood but because he came  here without actually having the power  of the founding Titan within him but  instead he entered this place because he  came into contact with Aaron's blood  Zeke was apparently able to overcome the  vow of pacifism which restrains all  other holders of the founding Titan with  royal blood and while our information on  Emir Fritz and the coordinate is by no  means complete the fact that Zeke is  able to overcome the valve pacifism is a  huge reveal also the fact that he mere  fritz  the legendary progenitor is actually a  slave without a will of her own is  shocking to say the least I still don't  quite believe it personally I think that  this Amir who is a slave and who no  longer has a will of her own may just be  one part of Amir fritz some small part  of her that didn't die when her physical  body died but I find it hard to believe  that the legendary Amir was always  nothing but a slave although if that is  then it is clear that everything we  think we know about the history of the  attack on Titan world is completely  wrong we now know that all LD ins are  connected by the paths we know that all  these paths come together at the  coordinate and we know that the  coordinates visual representation is an  unknown land beyond space and time which  features a giant tree-like pillar of  light and Amir frits who seemingly  wanders without a will of her own and  uses the soil to construct and  reconstruct Titans because the paths  transcend both space and time  Titan transformations are able to  violate the laws of science by allowing  physical material to be transported  instantly from